course: dictionary
lesson: 5973
title: Maximum: the most possible
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Maximum means the most that is possible or allowed. Its opposite is minimum, which means the least. The word can be a noun, an adjective or, in informal speech, an adverb.
explain: As a noun, «the maximum is 30 pupils» means that 30 is the largest number allowed. As an adjective, «maximum speed» means the greatest speed, and «maximum score» means the highest score you can get.
explain: After a number, informal speech uses maximum to mean "at most". «It'll take ten minutes maximum» means ten minutes or less. Check the clues around the word, and you can work out which meaning is used.
fact: Maximum means the largest amount, number or size that is possible or allowed.
fact: The opposite of maximum is minimum, the smallest amount possible.
fact: In maths, the range of a set of data is the maximum minus the minimum.
fact: A maximum thermometer records the highest temperature.
fact: «Maximum» after a number means "at most", as in «two hours maximum». Informal "to the max" means as much as possible.
exercise: «The maximum is 30 pupils.» What does maximum mean in this sentence? | The least number allowed | *The largest number allowed | A number that is wrong | The number of teachers in the room
exercise: «The sign shows the maximum speed on this road.» What does maximum speed mean? | The slowest speed | The speed of a bus | The speed of the wind | *The highest speed allowed
exercise: «It'll take ten minutes maximum.» What does maximum mean here? | At least an hour | *Ten minutes at most, or less | Ten minutes exactly | Ten extra minutes
test: In a set of numbers, the maximum is 9 and the minimum is 2. What is the range? | 5 | *7 | 11 | 18
test: Which instrument records the highest temperature? | *A maximum thermometer | A ruler | A compass | A clock
exam: Jayden says «I'll revise to the max» before his test. What does "to the max" mean? | *As much as possible | Quietly | Only a little | Not at all
